Sinew dataset & code — licensing
=================================

COMPILATION (the dataset: schema, derived tables, build pipeline, and the curated assembly
of cross-references): Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0).
SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

REQUIRED ATTRIBUTION
--------------------
Cross-reference connections are derived from OpenBible.info and are licensed CC-BY. Any
redistribution or use MUST credit:
  "Cross-references © OpenBible.info, CC-BY (https://www.openbible.info/labs/cross-references/)."
The BLIVRE (pt-BR) text in the `texts` table is licensed CC BY 4.0 Brasil. Any redistribution
or use of that text MUST credit:
  "Todas as Escrituras em português citadas são da Bíblia Livre (BLIVRE), Copyright ©
  Diego Santos, Mario Sérgio, e Marco Teles, http://sites.google.com/site/biblialivre/ —
  Licença Creative Commons Atribuição 4.0 Brasil."
The NVA (pt-BR) text in the `texts` table is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. Any redistribution or use
of that text MUST credit:
  "Todas as Escrituras em português citadas (tradução NVA) são da Nova Bíblia de Acesso Livre,
  https://www.biblianva.com.br/ — Licença Creative Commons Atribuição-CompartilhaIgual 4.0."
In all cases, also acknowledge this dataset:
  "Sinew — sourced Bible connection-graph (CC-BY-4.0)."

NOTE ON NVA / CC BY-SA — SCOPE OF SHAREALIKE (resolved 2026-08-26): CC BY-SA 4.0's ShareAlike
clause (Section 3(b)) only triggers on "Adapted Material" — Section 1 defines that as material
"in which the Licensed Material is translated, altered, arranged, transformed, or otherwise
modified." CC's own FAQ (creativecommons.org/faq, "Combining and adapting CC material") states a
collection where licensed material appears "in unmodified form alongside other material" is NOT
an adaptation, and ShareAlike does not extend to the rest of such a collection. `text_pt.load_nva`
does not translate/alter/transform the NVA text — it whitespace-normalizes and subsets which
verses are included (by membership in the WEB-derived canonical set), verbatim otherwise. On that
basis, the NVA text sits in this compilation as a Collection component, not an Adaptation: the
CC-BY-4.0 compilation license above stands as written, and ShareAlike binds only the NVA text
itself (any future adaptation of the NVA text specifically — e.g. rewording it — would need to
carry CC BY-SA 4.0 forward). This is a careful non-lawyer reading of the primary sources, not
legal advice — revisit if the NVA text ever gets transformed rather than merely subset/included.

UNDERLYING TEXT
---------------
The World English Bible (WEB) text is in the PUBLIC DOMAIN and carries no usage restrictions.
The Bíblia Livre (BLIVRE, N4 edition) text is licensed CC BY 4.0 Brasil — see REQUIRED
ATTRIBUTION above. Source: https://github.com/blivre/BibliaLivre (release 2018.2.0).
The Nova Bíblia de Acesso Livre (NVA) text is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 — see REQUIRED ATTRIBUTION
above (including the ShareAlike-scope note). Source: https://www.biblianva.com.br/,
fetched via https://github.com/Projeto-Euaggelion/biblia.publica (aggregator).

VERSIFICATION
-------------
Versification mappings adopt the Copenhagen Alliance versification specification
(https://github.com/Copenhagen-Alliance/versification-specification), CC-BY / open license.

Per-source URLs and sha256 pins are recorded in sources.lock.json and in the dataset_meta table.
